---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const lastUpdated = 'November 8, 2026';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy | Odiuko Educational Services">
  <main class="privacy">
    <div class="inner">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <p>
        Odiuko Educational Services ("Odiuko", "we", "us") provides tutoring and
        learning support. This policy explains what personal information we collect,
        why we collect it, and the choices you have. We handle personal data in line
        with the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023 (NDPA).
      </p>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Odiuko Educational Services is the data controller for the information
        described here. You can reach us at
        <a href="mailto:info@odiuko.ng">info@odiuko.ng</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
      <p>Depending on how you use our services, we may collect:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Parent or guardian details: name, phone number, email address, and location (for in-home tutoring).</li>
        <li>Child details: name, age, class or grade level, school, and learning needs or goals you choose to share.</li>
        <li>Messages and enquiries you send us by email, WhatsApp, or our contact forms.</li>
        <li>Learning information: progress notes, assessments, and feedback from sessions.</li>
        <li>Basic website data, such as pages visited and device or browser type.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not ask for more information than we need to provide the service.</p>

      <h2>3. Why we use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To respond to enquiries and arrange tutoring or school services.</li>
        <li>To plan and deliver lessons that fit each child's needs.</li>
        <li>To share progress updates with parents or guardians.</li>
        <li>To manage scheduling, communication, and (where applicable) payments.</li>
        <li>To keep our website secure and improve it.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We rely on your consent, on the need to provide a service you have asked for,
        and on our legitimate interest in running and improving our services.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Children's information</h2>
      <p>
        Our tutoring services are for children, so we collect a child's information
        only from, or with the consent of, a parent or guardian. If you believe we
        hold a child's information without a parent's or guardian's consent, contact
        us and we will remove it.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell personal information. We share it only where necessary, for
        example with a school you have asked us to work with, or with service
        providers who help us run our website, email, and communication tools. These
        providers may only use the information to help us deliver our services.
        Messages sent through WhatsApp are also subject to WhatsApp's own terms and
        privacy policy. We may also disclose information where the law requires it.
      </p>

      <h2>6. How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep personal information only for as long as we need it for the purposes
        above, or as the law requires. When it is no longer needed, we delete it or
        make it anonymous.
      </p>

      <h2>7. How we protect it</h2>
      <p>
        We take reasonable technical and organisational steps to protect personal
        information from loss, misuse, and unauthorised access. No online system is
        completely secure, but we work to limit access to those who need it.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under the NDPA, you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Ask what personal information we hold about you or your child.</li>
        <li>Ask us to correct information that is wrong or incomplete.</li>
        <li>Ask us to delete your information, or to stop using it, in certain circumstances.</li>
        <li>Withdraw your consent at any time.</li>
        <li>Object to certain uses of your information.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To use any of these rights, email us at
        <a href="mailto:info@odiuko.ng">info@odiuko.ng</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Complaints</h2>
      <p>
        If you are not happy with how we handle your information, please contact us
        first and we will try to put it right. You also have the right to complain to
        the Nigeria Data Protection Commission (NDPC).
      </p>

      <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top shows when
        it was last changed.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Odiuko Educational Services<br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:info@odiuko.ng">info@odiuko.ng</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .privacy {
    background: #F8F3E3;
    color: #3a2f12;
    padding: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 4rem) clamp(1.25rem, 5vw, 4rem);
  }

  .privacy .inner {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .privacy h1 {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 5vw, 2.6rem);
    color: #6F5720;
    margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
  }

  .privacy h2 {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 3vw, 1.4rem);
    color: #6F5720;
    margin: 2rem 0 0.5rem;
  }

  .privacy p,
  .privacy li {
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .privacy ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .privacy li {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .privacy .updated {
    opacity: 0.7;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .privacy a {
    color: #6F5720;
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
